# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# This is not a style preference. Several guards in this repository compare text:
# scripts/fidelity.mjs checks that a block quoted in a standard is byte-faithful to the source
# specification, scripts/diagrams.mjs compares a Mermaid source against its embedded copy, and
# attestation staleness is a content digest over reviewed files. If line endings depended on which
# platform last touched a file, those comparisons would fail — or worse, a digest would change with
# no change to the content, and someone would learn to ignore the resulting noise.
#
# eol=lf rather than eol=native for the same reason: identical content must digest identically on
# every machine that runs the checks.
* text=auto eol=lf
